<section class="statement section-py-sm" aria-labelledby="statement-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <hr class="divider" />
    <div class="statement-inner">
      <h2 class="statement-heading" id="statement-heading">
        I like building things<br />
        that are hard to break.
      </h2>
      <div class="statement-body">
        <p>
          Backend engineering is about more than making code work — it's about
          designing systems that stay reliable under pressure, scale without
          accumulating fragility, and remain understandable as they grow.
        </p>
        <p>
          I work across APIs, databases, distributed systems, authentication
          infrastructure, and backend architecture. I'm interested in the
          decisions that matter: data consistency, failure modes, service
          boundaries, and how systems behave at their edges.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .statement {
    padding-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }

  .statement-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 4rem;
    align-items: start;
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  .statement-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.8rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .statement-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .statement-body p {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .statement-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
